FACT food_tithe.the_third_year(one_tithe_not_two) = ("one tithe not two (14:28) — the poor man's tithe replaces the second in the third and the sixth year (the Sifrei 109:5, 109:10-11; Rosh Hashanah 12b:1-5), the Levite never interrupted (KO.the_tithe by CALL): THE WRITE poor_tithe_owed — a STATUS on Israel at the chapter's own day; the readback row 14:28 SUPPLIED AS A LAW with its write", ['poor_tithe_owed'], [('INK', 'Deut 14:28 — "AT THE END OF THREE YEARS you shall bring out all the tithe of your yield in that year" — "at the end of three years" [\'2Kgs 18:10\', \'Deut 14:28\'] (2 Kings 18:10 Samaria\'s fall the one kin); the parser\'s [3] [3] and the starred token [\'שנים*\', \'מעשר*\']; "the tithe of your yield" [\'Deut 14:28\', \'Deut 26:12\'] (14:28, 26:12)'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 109:5, 109:10-11 (read whole at the reading); Rosh Hashanah 12b:1-5 (read whole at the docket); cold_run_korach (CALL) — KO.the_tithe(third_year) = the first tithe every year — juxtaposed to an inheritance (R; the tape (the recon): portion_declared at Num 18:20 — ONE TITHE NOT TWO — in the third and the sixth year the poor man's tithe REPLACES the second (109:5, 109:10-11; Rosh Hashanah 12b:1-2 — the second year into the third, 'the year of THE tithe'); THE LEVITE NEVER INTERRUPTED — the first tithe every year: R. Yehuda from 14:29's Levite, R. Eliezer ben Yaakov from the inheritance's juxtaposition (12b:4-5; KO.the_tithe 'third_year' by CALL — already a move there)"), ('DATA', "THE WRITE poor_tithe_owed — a NEW STATUS on israel_people at the counter's day (40, 11, 1) (DF2, DF4; the one database on Israel []); the readback row 14:28 SUPPLIED AS A LAW WITH THE WRITE (the kin by CALL — yovel, korach); the Levite's first tithe unmoved")])
FACT food_tithe.the_third_year(the_levite_never_interrupted) = ("the Levite never interrupted (14:29) — the first tithe every year, the third too (Rosh Hashanah 12b:4 — R. Yehuda from 'and the Levite shall come', R. Eliezer ben Yaakov from the inheritance): the Levite in the third year accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 14:29 — "AND THE LEVITE, because he has no portion or inheritance with you" — "and the Levite shall come" [\'Deut 14:29\'] (one seat); the clause of 14:27 said again [\'Deut 14:27\', \'Deut 14:29\']'), ('MOVE', "Rosh Hashanah 12b:4 (read whole at the docket); cold_run_korach (CALL) — KO.the_tithe(tithe_to_levites) = all the tithe in Israel — in exchange for their service (18: — THE LEVITE NEVER INTERRUPTED — the first tithe is separated every year, the third included: R. Yehuda from 'and the Levite … shall come' (14:29 — he comes for what is his), R. Eliezer ben Yaakov from the juxtaposition to an inheritance ('as an inheritance does not cease, so the first tithe' — 12b:4; KO by CALL: the Levite serves, the Levite takes)"), ('DATA', "the Levite never interrupted a DATA row (the_levite_never_interrupted — Rosh Hashanah 12b:4); the exam's person the Levite in the third year — accepted (his first tithe)")])
FACT food_tithe.the_third_year(the_removal_date) = ("the removal's date (14:28) — the eve of the last festival day of Passover of the fourth and the seventh year (Mishnah Maaser Sheni 5:6; the Sifrei 109:1-3 — I2 with 31:10): THE PARAMETER the_removal_date, the date the calendar's own key; the one who removes the tithes on that eve accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 14:28 — "at the END of three years" — "at the end" in the book [\'Deut 13:8\', \'Deut 14:28\', \'Deut 15:1\', \'Deut 28:49\', \'Deut 28:64\', \'Deut 31:10\', \'Deut 9:11\'] (15:1, 31:10 the seven years\' twins: "at the end of seven years" [\'Deut 15:1\', \'Deut 31:10\', \'Jer 34:14\'])'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 109:1-3 (read whole at the reading — I2 with 31:10, checked in MIDDOT.md); Mishnah Maaser Sheni 5:6 (read whole at the docket); cold_run_korach (CALL) — KO.the_tithe(removal) = the removal on Passover eve of the fourth and seventh years — the firs; the parameter the_removal_date = ['one_tithe_not_two', 'the_eve', 'the_uses', 'the_years']; the calendar's keys passover_1 {'month': 1, 'day': 15}, passover_7 {'from': 'passover_1', 'plus': 6} — THE REMOVAL'S DATE A CLOCK DATUM — 'at the end of three years' read with 31:10's 'at the end of seven years, at the festival' (I2): the eve of the last festival day of Passover of the fourth and the seventh year the time of removal (Mishnah Maaser Sheni 5:6; 109:1-3); KO.the_tithe 'removal' the first tithe's side; the date rendered by the calendar's own keys (passover_7's eve), never a constant; 26:12 ahead the confession's seat"), ('DATA', "THE PARAMETER the_removal_date on file (DF6 — ['one_tithe_not_two', 'the_eve', 'the_uses', 'the_years']; the eve's key passover_7 the calendar's); the exam's person the one who removes the tithes on the eve of the last festival day of Passover of the fourth year — accepted")])
FACT food_tithe.the_third_year(the_seventh_year_by_the_cycle) = ("the seventh year by the cycle (14:28) — the third and the sixth work years, the seventh the sabbath of the land (YO.cycle by CALL; CA.sabbatical 'land released in year 7'; the Sifrei 109:4): the one who would tithe the seventh year's produce exempt", ['exempt'], [('INK', 'Deut 14:28 — "in that year" — the third of the count; the kin\'s numbers by the parser: 15:1 [7], 31:10 [7], Exodus 23:10 [6]'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 109:4 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_yovel (CALL) — YO.cycle(3) = work_year, YO.cycle(6) = work_year, YO.cycle(7) = sabbath_of_the_land, YO.cycle(50) = jubilee; cold_run_calendar (CALL) — CA.sabbatical(timer) = land released in year 7 — THE YEARS BY CALL TO THE CYCLE — the third and the sixth of the count work years (the poor man's tithe's), the seventh THE SABBATH OF THE LAND (yovel.cycle by CALL: no tithe — the seventh year's produce ownerless, 109:4; Exodus 23:10-11 through its spine — calendar.sabbatical 'land released in year 7'); THE CELL READS THE COUNT'S YEAR FROM THE CYCLE, never a constant; on the bare world before the entry the count not begun (the running world's count read at the tape)"), ('DATA', "the seventh year by the cycle a DATA row (the_seventh_year_by_the_cycle — YO.cycle(3, 6, 7, 50) by CALL; CA.sabbatical); the exam's person the one who would tithe the seventh year's produce — EXEMPT (no tithe in the sabbath of the land)")])
FACT food_tithe.the_third_year(the_tithes_new_year) = ("the tithes' new year (14:28) — Tishri 1 with the first third beside it, the tree's the fifteenth of Shevat (Rosh Hashanah 12a:6-9, 12b:9-11, 13a:3; Mishnah Rosh Hashanah 1:1): THE PARAMETER the_tithes_new_year; the one who tithes by the first third accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 14:28 — "in that year" — the year\'s bound; the tithes\' new year the parameter [\'shevat_15\', \'the_first_third\', \'tishri_1\', \'year_by_year\']; the calendar\'s key rosh_hashanah {\'month\': 7, \'day\': 1}'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 109:8 (read whole at the reading); Rosh Hashanah 12a:6-9, 12b:9-11, 13a:3-13 (read whole at the docket); Mishnah Rosh Hashanah 1:1; Bekhorot 53b:5 — THE TITHES' NEW YEAR A CLOCK DATUM — Tishri 1 for the tithes (Mishnah Rosh Hashanah 1:1's four new years; 12a:6-9 'tithes' plural — the animal's and the grain's); THE FIRST THIRD — produce that reached a third of its growth before Tishri 1 belongs to the year that closed (12b:9-11; 13a:3 from 31:10's festival of gathering; Joshua's omer (the sheaf) 13a:7-13 — departure (i)); the vegetables by the picking (109:8); the tree's the fifteenth of Shevat"), ('DATA', "THE PARAMETER the_tithes_new_year on file (DF6 — ['shevat_15', 'the_first_third', 'tishri_1', 'year_by_year']; the key rosh_hashanah the calendar's); the exam's person the one who tithes grain that reached a third before Tishri as the old year's — accepted")])
FACT food_tithe.the_third_year(the_gifts_exempt) = ('the gifts exempt (14:28-29) — the corner, the gleanings and the forgotten sheaf owe no tithe (the Sifrei 109:12; HO.gifts by CALL — the window until the smoothing; the import table names 14:28): the owner who leaves the corner and does not tithe it — left for the poor', ['left_for_the_poor'], [('INK', 'Deut 14:28-29 — "and lay it up WITHIN YOUR GATES … the sojourner and the fatherless and the widow who are in your gates" — "in your gates" at 14:28-29 [28, 29]; the corner\'s clause 24:19\'s "for the sojourner, the fatherless and the widow" [\'Deut 24:19\', \'Deut 24:20\', \'Deut 24:21\', \'Deut 26:12\']'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 109:12 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_holiness (CALL) — HO.gifts(recipients) = the_poor_and_the_convert_not_the_resident_alien; HO.gifts(window_end) = until_the_smoothing; HO.gifts(copy_23_22) = the_Emor_copy_omits_the_vineyard; HO.GIFTS_IMPORT = {'forgotten_sheaf': 'Deut 24:19', 'forgotten_olive': 'Deut 24:20', 'poor_tithe': 'Deut 14:28'}; cold_run_moadim (CALL) — MO.law_moadim(harvest_reaped) -> barred_from_it — THE GIFTS EXEMPT FROM THE TITHE — the gleanings, the forgotten sheaf and the corner owe no tithe (109:12; Leviticus 19:9-10 by CALL — left_for_the_poor the effect; Mishnah Peah 1:6 the window until the smoothing — HO 'window_end'); THE LEVITICUS RUNNER'S IMPORT TABLE ALREADY POINTS AT 14:28 (GIFTS_IMPORT's poor_tithe — the reverse edge on file); 23:22 the Emor copy without the vineyard (HO 'copy_23_22'); the moadim daemon's harvest branch by CALL (the new grain until the omer — 23:14)"), ('DATA', "the gifts exempt a DATA row (the_gifts_exempt — 109:12; HO.gifts by CALL; GIFTS_IMPORT names 14:28); the readback row 14:29 EXPANDED (holiness.gifts, second_tablets by CALL; stranger_love_commanded Deut 10:17 by kind); the exam's person the owner who leaves the corner and does not tithe it — left_for_the_poor")])
