FACT food_tithe.the_third_year(the_courtyard_from_your_gates) = ("the courtyard from 'your gates' (14:29) — the liability by the house (R. Yannai) or the courtyard (R. Yochanan, from 'in your gates') — Bava Metzia 88a:1-2; KO.the_tithe 'thresholds' by CALL: the one whose produce entered the courtyard through its gate accepted as liable", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 14:29 — "who are IN YOUR GATES shall come and eat" — "in your gates" at 14:29 True'), ('MOVE', "Bava Metzia 88a:1-2 (read whole at the docket); cold_run_korach (CALL) — KO.the_tithe(thresholds) = the pile evened, the wine skimmed, the oil dripped (Sifrei 121:1; Mish — THE LIABILITY BY THE HOUSE OR THE COURTYARD FROM 14:29'S OWN PHRASE — 'in your gates': produce that entered through the courtyard's gate is liable to the tithe (Bava Metzia 88a:1-2 — R. Yannai: untithed produce is not liable until it sees the front of the house, from 26:13's 'I have removed the holy from the house'; R. Yochanan: even the courtyard, from 'in your gates'); the thresholds the pile smoothed (KO 'thresholds' by CALL — departure (g): korach's cell carries the courtyard's arm)"), ('DATA', 'the courtyard from "your gates" a DATA row (the_courtyard_from_your_gates — Bava Metzia 88a:1-2; departure (g)); the exam\'s person the one whose produce entered the courtyard through its gate — accepted (liable)')])
