e cell by CALL")])
FACT food_tithe.the_far_place_the_money_the_rejoicing_and_the_levite(the_levites_ladder) = ("the Levite's ladder (14:27) — 'you shall not forsake him' with four sources (10:9, 12:12, 12:19, Numbers 18:20-24 by CALL — ST, PN, KO; 14:29 the fourth; the Sifrei 108:1): levite_forsaking_barred REUSED — a second entry on Israel (12:19's the first)", ['levite_forsaking_barred'], [('INK', 'Deut 14:27 — "AND THE LEVITE who is in your gates, YOU SHALL NOT FORSAKE HIM, for he has no portion or inheritance with you" — "the Levite who is in your gates" [\'Deut 12:18\', \'Deut 14:27\', \'Deut 16:11\'] (12:18, 14:27, 16:11); "he has no portion or inheritance with you" [\'Deut 14:27\', \'Deut 14:29\'] (14:27, 14:29); "portion and inheritance" the Bible\'s 6; the shared run with 12:19 0 (no token — the reuse by the law, not the words)'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 108:1 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_place_name (CALL) — PN.the_profane_slaughter_the_blood_and_the_gates(lest_you_forsake_the_levite) = lest you forsake the Levite (12:19) — the verse al; PN(the_levites_scope) = the Levite's scope (12:19) — 'all your days' even ; cold_run_second_tablets (CALL) — ST.the_levites_separated(levi_has_no_portion) = Levi has no portion (10:9) — the tape's portion_de; cold_run_korach (CALL) — KO.the_tithe(no_inheritance) = in their land you shall not inherit — I am your po; the tape (the recon): portion_declared at Num 18:20 (the-levites) — THE LADDER OF FOUR — 'you shall not forsake him' a status with four sources: 10:9 (the Levites separated — ST by CALL), 12:12 and 12:19 (PN by CALL — 'all your days' even in sabbaticals, 'on your land' not in the exile), Numbers 18:20-24 (KO by CALL — portion_declared on the tape; inheritance_barred and tithe_granted the Levites' entries UNMOVED), 14:29 the fourth (108:1); levite_forsaking_barred REUSED — 12:19's block on Israel written A SECOND TIME at 14:27 (a second entry; DD2's and Q32's ONE retyped TWO, the blocks 4 -> 5)"), ('DATA', "THE REUSE levite_forsaking_barred — a SECOND ENTRY on israel_people at the counter's day (40, 11, 1) on the line second_tithe_declared (DF2; REUSE_SCAN [['israel_people'], ['israel_people']]); tithe_granted and inheritance_barred ONE each on the Levites UNMOVED (DF5); the readback row 14:27 VERBATIM in kind (portion_declared Num 18:20) with the cells by CALL")])
FACT food_tithe.the_far_place_the_money_the_rejoicing_and_the_levite(shiloh_and_the_house) = ('Shiloh and the House (14:25) — the place which He will choose: Shiloh and the House of Eternity (the Sifrei 107:6; the eras table by CALL — PN.the_place_chosen): the one who brings the tithe to Shiloh in its era accepted', ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 14:25 — "and go to THE PLACE which the LORD your God will choose" — the formula [\'Deut 14:25\'] (one seat with "go"); the place formula in the book 11'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 107:6 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_place_name (CALL) — PN.the_place_chosen(the_place_which_the_lord_will_choose) = the place which the LORD will choose (12:5) — installed here; PN.the_place_chosen(the_stations_six_rows) = the stations' six rows (12:9-11) — the wilderness permitted  — SHILOH AND THE ETERNAL HOUSE — 'the place which He will choose' is Shiloh and the House of Eternity (107:6): THE ERAS TABLE BY CALL (the stations' six rows — chapter 12's cell reads them, this chapter reads the cell); the formula's fourth and fifth seats here (14:23-25)"), ('DATA', "Shiloh and the House a DATA row (shiloh_and_the_house — 107:6; the eras table by CALL); the readback rows 14:23 and 14:25 the formula's seats by CALL; the exam's person the one who brings the tithe to Shiloh in its era — accepted")])
