FACT release_firstborn.the_needy_and_the_blessing(the_needy_condition) = ("the needy's condition (15:4, 15:11) — 'there shall be no needy among you' when you do His will, 'the needy shall never cease' when you do not (the Sifrei 114:1, 118:1 — the two verses upheld by a condition, no third verse): A STATE VARIABLE with two arms; 15:4 a precedence rule for one's own property (Bava Metzia 33a:10): the reader who asks whether the needy cease accepted — the arm from the world's state", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:4 — "HOWBEIT there shall be NO NEEDY among you" against 15:11 "for the needy shall NEVER CEASE from the land" — the two verses share 3 tokens in order; "needy" the Torah\'s nine tokens [\'Deut 15:4\', \'Deut 15:7\', \'Deut 15:7\', \'Deut 15:9\', \'Deut 15:11\', \'Deut 15:11\', \'Deut 24:14\', \'Exod 23:6\', \'Exod 23:11\'] (six in this chapter); "howbeit" [\'2Sam 12:14\', \'Amos 6:10\', \'Amos 9:8\', \'Deut 15:4\', \'Gen 47:15\', \'Gen 47:16\', \'Isa 16:4\', \'Isa 29:20\', \'Isa 34:12\', \'Isa 41:29\', \'Isa 45:14\', \'Isa 45:6\', \'Isa 54:15\', \'Isa 5:8\', \'Judg 4:9\', \'Num 13:28\', \'Num 23:13\']; "cease" in the book [(\'Deut 15:11\', \'יחדל\'), (\'Deut 23:23\', \'תחדל\')]'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 114:1, 118:1 (read whole at the reading); Taanit 21a:2-4, Berakhot 34b:20, Shabbat 63a:10, Bava Metzia 30b:1, 33a:10, Sanhedrin 64b:15 (read whole at the docket) — THE TWO VERSES UPHELD BY A CONDITION, NOT A THIRD VERSE — 'there shall be no needy among you' WHEN YOU DO THE WILL OF THE OMNIPRESENT, 'the needy shall never cease' WHEN YOU DO NOT (114:1; 118:1 — I13's question asked and answered without its third verse: the condition 15:5's hearing): A STATE VARIABLE the_needy_condition with two arms, the cell returning the arm from the world's state; 15:4 read as A PRECEDENCE RULE for one's own property (Bava Metzia 30b:1, 33a:10 — 'howbeit there shall be no needy among you: yours before any man's'; Sanhedrin 64b:15); the two verses two lives (Taanit 21a:2-4); Shmuel's unchanged world (Berakhot 34b:20; Shabbat 63a:10)"), ('DATA', 'THE STATE ROW (the_needy_condition — two arms: the blessing\'s when the commandment is kept, the default "the needy shall never cease"; the readback row 15:4 the state row, SUPPLIED); the precedence rule for one\'s own property a second reading (Bava Metzia 33a); the exam\'s person the reader who asks whether the needy cease — the arm from the world\'s state: accepted')])
FACT release_firstborn.the_needy_and_the_blessing(the_blessing_in_the_land) = ("the blessing in the Land (15:4) — 'bless, He will bless you in the land … to possess it': only in the Land, and the conquest first (the Sifrei 114:2-3; 25:19's clause the twin): the settler who expects the blessing before the possession accepted — the blessing after it", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:4 — "for the LORD will BLESS, HE WILL BLESS you IN THE LAND which the LORD your God gives you for an inheritance to possess it" — "bless, He will bless you" [\'Deut 15:4\'] (one seat; Abraham\'s "bless, I will bless you" [\'Gen 22:17\'] the form\'s first); "for an inheritance to possess it" [\'Deut 15:4\', \'Deut 25:19\'] (25:19\'s twin); the doubling an infinitive absolute [\'ברך\']'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 114:2-3 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_blessing_and_curse (CALL) — BC.the_blessing_and_the_curse(keep_to_do) = keep to do (11:32) — 'keep to do all the statutes  — THE BLESSING ONLY IN THE LAND (114:2 — 'in the land': not outside it) and THE CONQUEST FIRST (114:3 — 'which the LORD your God gives you for an inheritance to possess it': as a reward for possessing it; the same clause at 25:19's Amalek); the doubled 'bless' the eighth infinitive absolute's first (the shelf's doublings)"), ('DATA', "the blessing in the Land a DATA row (the_blessing_in_the_land — 114:2-3; 25:19's clause); the exam's person the settler who expects the blessing before the conquest — the blessing after the possession: accepted")])
FACT release_firstborn.the_needy_and_the_blessing(the_hearkening) = ("the hearkening (15:5) — 'only if you diligently hearken': 28:1's header fourteen of seventeen in order, 11:13's conditional the same form (BC.the_second_paragraph by CALL): blessings_for_hearing REUSED — a second entry on Israel at the chapter's own day (7:12's the first); the one who hearkens diligently accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:5 — "ONLY IF YOU DILIGENTLY HEARKEN to the voice of the LORD your God, to keep to do all this commandment" — "if you diligently hearken" [\'Deut 15:5\', \'Deut 28:1\', \'Exod 15:26\'] (28:1\'s blessing header, Marah\'s Exodus 15:26); the shared run with 28:1 14 of 17; 11:13\'s plural [\'Deut 11:13\']; "all this commandment" in the book [\'Deut 11:22\', \'Deut 15:5\', \'Deut 19:9\', \'Deut 6:25\']; "only" at [5, 23]'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 115:1-2 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_blessing_and_curse (CALL) — BC.the_second_paragraph(if_you_hearken) = if you hearken (11:13) — the doubled infinitive's plural for; the one database: blessings_for_hearing on israel_people before this daemon's lines ['israel_people'] (7:12's line hearing_blessed) — blessings_for_hearing REUSED — chapter 7's conditional HEAVEN entry (7:12 'because you hear these judgments', the tape's hearing_blessed) written A SECOND TIME on israel_people at the chapter's own day: 15:5 'if you diligently hearken' 28:1's header (fourteen of seventeen in order), 11:13's second paragraph THE SAME FORM (the plural; BC by CALL); 8b's lesson: a reused effect is a second entry on the same ledger (CQ6's, DC6's, Q21's, Q30's ONE retyped TWO)"), ('DATA', "THE REUSE blessings_for_hearing — a second entry on israel_people on the line release_law_declared (DG2 — the running world held ONE, the count read from the one database by source); the readback row 15:5 VARIANT by CALL (second_paragraph_declared Deut 11:13 by kind; 28:1 ahead); the exam's person the one who hearkens diligently — accepted")])
FACT release_firstborn.the_needy_and_the_blessing(the_scribes_words) = ("the words of the scribes (15:5) — 'hear, you shall hear' the oral law named inside the spine (the Sifrei 115:1: the words of the scribes among the commandments); the light as the weighty (115:2): the one who keeps the words of the scribes as the commandment accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:5 — "hear, you shall hear … to keep to do ALL THIS COMMANDMENT which I command you today" — "to keep to do all this commandment" [\'Deut 15:5\'] (one seat); "which I command you today" in the book 18 seats; Moses\' "I" (אנכי) in the chapter [5, 11, 15]'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 115:1-2 (read whole at the reading) — THE WORDS OF THE SCRIBES NAMED at 'hear, you shall hear' (115:1 — 'if you hearken to the voice of the LORD your God': to the voice of the commandments, the words of the scribes among them: A DATA ROW the_scribes_words — the oral law's seat inside the spine); THE LIGHT AS THE WEIGHTY (115:2 — 'to keep to do all this commandment': a light commandment as a weighty one)"), ('DATA', "the words of the scribes a DATA row (the_scribes_words — 115:1); the light as the weighty (the_light_as_the_weighty — 115:2); the exam's person the one who keeps the words of the scribes as the commandment — accepted")])
FACT release_firstborn.the_needy_and_the_blessing(the_receipts_referent_ahead) = ("the receipt's referent ahead (15:6) — 'as He spoke to you' answered by 28:3 'blessed shall you be in the city' (the Sifrei 116:1), a verse not yet spoken: THE POINTER ROW with its referent ahead, graded H — a labeled hypothesis until 28:3's sitting; the finder finds no receipt (GL.receipt_seats by CALL): the scholar who reads it so accepted as a hypothesis", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:6 — "for the LORD your God has blessed you, AS HE SPOKE TO YOU" — "as He spoke to you" FOUR in the book [\'Deut 12:20\', \'Deut 15:6\', \'Deut 26:18\', \'Deut 29:12\'] (12:20\'s border, this, 26:18-19, 29:12); "as spoke" sixteen in the book; the finder\'s receipts at chapter 15 [] (none — the form is "commanded", not "spoke")'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 116:1 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_good_land (CALL) — GL.receipt_seats(15) = [], GL.the_frame(no_receipt) = no receipt (8:1-20) — the register gate' — THE RECEIPT'S REFERENT FORWARD — 116:1 answers 'as He spoke to you' with 28:3 'BLESSED SHALL YOU BE IN THE CITY AND BLESSED IN THE FIELD', a verse the book has not yet spoken: THE POINTER ROW OF THE READBACK WITH ITS REFERENT AHEAD, graded H — the receipt's third shape after the Name's and the back-pointer's, a labeled HYPOTHESIS until 28:3's sitting (no edge: the pointer row with the H flag); the finder finds no receipt here (12:20's was not one either)"), ('HYP', "THE POINTER ROW 15:6 -> 28:3 graded H — the referent AHEAD on the tape (28:3 not yet spoken): a labeled hypothesis, no teacher but the Sifrei's own citation forward (116:1); resolved at 28:3's sitting; the readback row 15:6 SUPPLIED with the pointer"), ('DATA', 'the receipt\'s referent ahead a DATA row (the_receipts_referent_ahead — 15:6 -> 28:3 by the Sifrei 116:1; the pointer row\'s H flag; the four "as He spoke to you" seats); the exam\'s person the scholar who reads "as He spoke to you" as 28:3 — accepted as a hypothesis (the H class, counted apart)')])
FACT release_firstborn.the_needy_and_the_blessing(lend_not_borrow) = ("lend not borrow, rule not be ruled (15:6) — 'you shall lend to many nations and not borrow' (the Sifrei 116:2-3; 28:12 the twin with 'lend' for 'pledge', 28:44 the reversal; Judges 1:7's Adoni-bezek the run's case): the nation that lends and does not borrow accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:6 — "and you shall LEND to many nations and you shall not BORROW, and you shall RULE over many nations and they shall not rule over you" — the pledge-verb\'s six seats in the Bible [(\'Deut 15:6\', \'והעבטת\'), (\'Deut 15:6\', \'תעבט\'), (\'Deut 15:8\', \'והעבט\'), (\'Deut 15:8\', \'תעביטנו\'), (\'Deut 24:10\', \'לעבט\'), (\'Joel 2:7\', \'יעבטון\')] (this chapter\'s four, 24:10, Joel 2:7); 28:12\'s twin with "lend" for "pledge" [\'והלוית\', \'גוים\', \'רבים\', \'ואתה\', \'לא\', \'תלוה\'], the shared run 6; "many nations" in the book [\'Deut 15:6\', \'Deut 28:12\', \'Deut 7:1\']; 28:44 the curse\'s reversal [\'הוא\', \'ילוך\', \'ואתה\', \'לא\', \'תלונו\']'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 116:2-3 (read whole at the reading); Judges 1:7 the run's case; cold_run_yovel (CALL) — YO.valuation(male, 30) = 50 (the sela and the shekel by the valuations' twenty gerah) — LEND NOT BORROW, RULE NOT BE RULED (116:2-3 — 'you shall lend to many nations': not one nation; 'you shall not borrow'; 'you shall rule': as Adoni-bezek's seventy kings under his table, Judges 1:7 the run's case); 28:12 THE TWIN with 'lend' (לוה) for 'pledge' (עבט) by CALL when it comes; 28:44 the curse's reversal; the pledge-verb this chapter's own word (24:10's pledge, Joel's locusts the other seats)"), ('DATA', "lend not borrow a DATA row (lend_not_borrow — 116:2-3; 28:12 the twin, 28:44 the reversal; Adoni-bezek); the exam's person the nation that lends and does not borrow — accepted")])
FACT release_firstborn.the_needy_and_the_blessing(the_registers_two_near_misses) = ("the register's two near misses (15:2, 15:6) — 'this is the word of the release' a singular footer noun after 'this', 'as He spoke to you' not 'commanded': each outside the finder's forms by one token; no register seat at chapter 15 (the reading's measurement; GL.receipt_seats by CALL): the finder that finds no receipt at 15:6 accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 15:2, 15:6 — "and THIS (זה) is the WORD (דבר) of the release" — the footer noun in the singular after "this", not "these"; "as He SPOKE (דבר) to you" — not "commanded": the finder\'s receipts at chapter 15 [] (the good-land runner\'s finder by CALL; the reading\'s finder found none — ch15_ink.py\'s H print); "and this is the manner of" [\'1Kgs 9:15\', \'Deut 15:2\', \'Deut 19:4\']'), ('MOVE', 'register_census.py\'s forms (read at the design: a receipt "as … commanded … the LORD", a header "these" + statutes/commandments/judgments); cold_run_good_land (CALL) — GL.receipt_seats(15) = [] — THE REGISTER\'S TWO NEAR MISSES — 15:2\'s \'and this is the word of the release\' (the footer noun in the singular after \'this\') and 15:6\'s \'as He spoke to you\' (not \'commanded\'): each outside the finder\'s forms BY ONE TOKEN (the box\'s (l) — the reading\'s measurement repeated at the tape: no receipt with the Name, no header, no footer, no count line at chapter 15; DECLARED unmoved)'), ('DATA', "the register's two near misses a DATA row (the_registers_two_near_misses — 15:2 and 15:6 each outside by one token; no seat at Deut 15; the reading's finder found the eight receipts before chapter 15 and none in it); the exam's person the finder that finds no receipt at 15:6 — accepted")])
