FACT place_name.the_profane_slaughter_the_blood_and_the_gates(the_two_tithes) = ("the two tithes (12:17) — the Levites' first tithe eaten in every place (Num 18:31 — KR.the_tithe('every_place') by CALL; tithe_granted unmoved) against the owner's second tithe at the place (12:17 the first seat; 14:22-26): the Levite who eats his tithe in a cemetery accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 12:17 — "the tithe of your grain, your wine and your oil" barred from the gates against Numbers 18:31 "you shall eat it IN EVERY PLACE, you and your households" — "in every place" [\'Amos 8:3\', \'Deut 12:13\', \'Num 18:31\', \'Prov 15:3\'] (Num 18:31 and Deut 12:13 — the same two tokens); "the tithe" in the chapter [6, 11, 17]'), ('MOVE', "the tape (the recon): tithe_of_the_tithe_commanded at Num 18:25-32 (the-levites — FOUND by kind and first verse); cold_run_korach (CALL) — KR.the_tithe(every_place) = in every place — even a cemetery (Sifrei 122:1; Yevamot 86b — R. Akiva, KR.the_tithe(exclusion_table) = priests (18:20), Levites (18:23), bondsm; the Sifrei 77:7-8 — THE TWO TITHES — Numbers 18:31's 'in every place' THE LEVITES' TITHE EATEN ANYWHERE, even in a cemetery (Sifrei Bamidbar 122:1; Yevamot 86b — KR by CALL; tithe_granted on the Levites UNMOVED) against 12:17's SECOND TITHE AT THE PLACE (the owner's, the first fruits' kin — 14:22-26); the Levites' tithe the first, the owner's the second: two tithes, two places; the tithe's joint owners (77:7-8)"), ('DATA', 'THE TWO TITHES a DATA row (the_two_tithes — asserted on the DB: Num 18:31 "in every place", Deut 12:17 the second tithe\'s first seat); the exam\'s person the Levite who eats his tithe in a cemetery — the first tithe anywhere: accepted (Sifrei Bamidbar 122:1)')])
FACT place_name.the_profane_slaughter_the_blood_and_the_gates(the_impure_tithes_warning) = ("the impure tithe's warning (12:15-17) — 12:15's 'the impure … within your gates' against 12:17's 'you may not eat within your gates' (Makkot 19b:3-7); 'too far' as any inability, one stride outside the wall (19b:9-13); the second tithe and the Temple (19a:3-10): the one who takes one stride outside the wall accepted — outside", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 12:15-17 — "THE IMPURE AND THE PURE may eat it … IN ALL YOUR GATES" (12:15) against "YOU MAY NOT EAT WITHIN YOUR GATES the tithe" (12:17) — "your gates" in the chapter [12, 15, 17, 18, 21]; 12:21\'s "too far" [\'Deut 12:21\', \'Deut 14:24\']'), ('MOVE', "Makkot 19b:3-7, 19b:9-13, 19a:3-5, 19a:7, 19a:10 (read whole at the docket) — THE IMPURE TITHE'S WARNING FROM THE CHAPTER'S OWN GATES — the warning for eating the second tithe in impurity read from 12:15's 'the impure … within your gates' against 12:17's 'you may not eat within your gates' (19b:3-7 — the tithe eaten in your gates when impure is the profane's permission, barred for the tithe); 'TOO FAR' AS ANY INABILITY — 'when the place is too far … unable to carry it' (14:24): one stride outside the wall (19b:9-13 — 'from you' from your fullness); THE SECOND TITHE AND THE TEMPLE — juxtaposed to the firstborn at 14:23 (19a:3-5); the common element refuted (19a:7 — I3); the chain rule (19a:10)"), ('DATA', "the impure tithe's warning the docket's crown (D2b — the chapter's own gates the source); the exam's person the one who takes one stride outside the wall with the tithe — outside (19b:9-13): accepted")])
FACT place_name.the_profane_slaughter_the_blood_and_the_gates(lest_you_forsake_the_levite) = ("lest you forsake the Levite (12:19) — the verse alone in the Bible; a prohibition by 'take heed … lest' (the Sifrei 74:6-7): THE WRITE levite_forsaking_barred — a BLOCK on Israel at the chapter's own day; the readback row SUPPLIED AS A LAW with its write", ['levite_forsaking_barred'], [('INK', 'Deut 12:19 — "TAKE HEED TO YOURSELF LEST YOU FORSAKE THE LEVITE all your days on your land" — the verse ALONE in the Bible: "lest you forsake the Levite" the one seat [\'Deut 12:19\']; "all your days" [\'1Kgs 3:13\', \'Deut 12:19\', \'Deut 23:7\']; "on your land" [\'Deut 12:19\']; the Levite\'s seats in the chapter [12, 18]'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 74:6-7 (read whole at the reading); Pesachim 8b:7-9 (credited from 9b's docket) — THE LEVITE — a prohibition by the shelf's reading of 'take heed … lest' (74:6-7 — 'take heed' a negative command, 'lest' a negative command); the Levite's pilgrimage (Pesachim 8b — the Levite with no land and the pilgrimage's guard); the Levite within your gates at the rejoicing (12:12, 12:18 — the dearer first); 'no portion nor inheritance' (18:20 — portion_declared on the tape) the reason"), ('DATA', "THE WRITE levite_forsaking_barred — a BLOCK on israel_people at the counter's day (DD2, DD4): the code's hole compiled; the readback row 12:19 SUPPLIED AS A LAW WITH THE WRITE (the verse alone in the Bible — a DATA row)")])
FACT place_name.the_profane_slaughter_the_blood_and_the_gates(before_the_lord_you_shall_eat_it) = ("before the LORD you shall eat it (12:18) — the place (Shiloh and Jerusalem — the Sifrei 74:2-3), the household 5:14's (CH.the_first_tablet by CALL — the readback row VERBATIM in kind), the dearer first (74:4): the one who eats the second tithe in his gates accepted against — the place alone", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 12:18 — "BUT BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD YOU SHALL EAT IT, in the place which the LORD your God will choose — you and your son and your daughter, your manservant and your maidservant, and the Levite within your gates — and you shall rejoice before the LORD your God in all that you put your hand to" — the singular list [\'Deut 12:18\', \'Deut 16:11\', \'Deut 16:14\']; the shared run with 16:11 13 (THIRTEEN — the chapter\'s closest kin), with 5:14 8'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_covenant_at_horeb (CALL) — CH.the_first_tablet(the_servants_rest) = the servants' rest (5:14) — the circumcised slave ; the Sifrei 74:2-4; Makkot 19b:15 — 'BEFORE THE LORD YOU SHALL EAT IT' — Shiloh and Jerusalem (74:2-3 — the place's two names at the eating); the dearer first (74:4 — the son before the servant, the Levite last); 5:14's household said again (CH.the_first_tablet by CALL — the readback row 12:18 VERBATIM in kind); the bar's onset at the wall (Makkot 19b:15 — 12:18 read with 12:17); 16:11's thirteen tokens the feast's own"), ('DATA', "the readback row 12:18 — VERBATIM in kind by CALL (CH.the_first_tablet — 5:14's list); the rejoicing's status by kind (12:7's write); the exam's person the one who eats the second tithe in his gates before the pilgrimage — the place alone: accepted against")])
