FACT second_tablets.the_god_of_gods_and_the_stranger(seventy_persons) = ("seventy persons (10:22) — the Joseph runner's count by CALL (JS.seventy — Genesis 46:27's seventy, Exodus 1:5's restatement, Jochebed the seventieth, Bava Batra 123b:1): the readback row VERBATIM in kind; 'as the stars of heaven for multitude' 1:10's phrase (no cell — a DATA row by the ink); the register seat NONE with the compile's why", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 10:22 — "WITH SEVENTY PERSONS your fathers went down to Egypt, and now the LORD your God HAS MADE YOU AS THE STARS OF HEAVEN FOR MULTITUDE" — the parser [70]; "with seventy persons" the one seat [\'Deut 10:22\'] against Exodus 1:5\'s "seventy persons" [\'Exod 1:5\'] and Genesis 46:27\'s "all the persons … seventy" (the parser at 46:27 [2, 70], 1:5 [70]); "as the stars of heaven for multitude" the book\'s three [\'Deut 10:22\', \'Deut 1:10\', \'Deut 28:62\'] (1:10, 10:22, 28:62 — 1:10 no number); "made you" [(\'Deut 10:22\', \'שמך\'), (\'Exod 2:14\', \'שמך\')] (10:22 and Exodus 2:14\'s "who made you a prince" the verb\'s pair); the shared run with 1:10 4 [\'ככוכבי\', \'השמים\', \'לרב\'], 28:62 3, Genesis 46:27 2, Exodus 1:5 1'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_joseph (CALL) — JS.seventy(seventy) = 70; JS.seventy(exodus_seventy) = 70; JS.seventy(jochebed) = jochebed_born_between_the_walls; JS.seventy(diverge) = DIVERGE_leah_33_vs_32_living — the seventy counted at Genesis 46:27 and restated at Exodus 1:5 — the Joseph runner's cell; JOCHEBED THE SEVENTIETH (Bava Batra 123b:1 — R. Chama bar Chanina: conceived on the way, born between the walls, 'whom she bore to Levi in Egypt', Numbers 26:59); Dinah's twin the refuted arm (123a:21 — 'with' extends, E1 checked in MIDDOT.md); the sixty-six and the four answers"), ('DATA', 'the readback row 10:22 VERBATIM in kind by CALL — THE SEVENTY\'S THREE FORMS a DATA row (Genesis 46:27\'s order, Exodus 1:5\'s, 10:22\'s "with seventy persons"); 1:10\'s "as the stars of heaven for multitude" (four tokens shared) NO CELL in the opening-speech runner (the callees\' print — the design\'s opening_speech edge DROPPED, 6b\'s lesson: the phrase\'s three book seats a DATA row by the ink); THE REGISTER\'S COUNT SEAT Deut 10:22 kept NONE with the compile\'s why (the cell by CALL, no row on the population table — Exodus 1:5\'s form); Onkelos "בשבעין נפשן" (with seventy souls)')])
FACT second_tablets.the_god_of_gods_and_the_stranger(takes_no_bribe) = ("takes no bribe (10:17) — Exodus 23:8's block never written on the tape (OR.courts by CALL — bribe_barred asserted absent; 16:19 the command's seat forward): a declaration; the shelf's exam — a bribe even to judge truly (Ketubot 105a:10), the bribe blinds a fortiori (105a:16, I1); the judge who takes to judge truly accepted against", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 10:17 — "AND TAKES NO BRIBE" — "and takes no bribe" [\'Deut 10:17\'] (the one seat — God\'s); the bribe-lemma\'s six Torah tokens [(\'Deut 10:17\', \'שחד\'), (\'Deut 16:19\', \'שחד\'), (\'Deut 16:19\', \'השחד\'), (\'Deut 27:25\', \'שחד\'), (\'Exod 23:8\', \'ושחד\'), (\'Exod 23:8\', \'השחד\')]: Exodus 23:8\'s prohibition "and a bribe you shall not take" [\'Exod 23:8\'], 16:19\'s "you shall not take a bribe" [\'Deut 16:19\'] (the command\'s seat forward), 27:25\'s curse "who takes a bribe"'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_ordinances (CALL) — OR.courts(bribe) = the_bribed_judges_eyes_dim; OR.courts(bribe_absolute) = even_to_judge_truly — Exodus 23:8's BLOCK bribe_barred on the judge — NEVER WRITTEN ON THE TAPE (the one database: ['israel_people']; asserted at DB7 — 10:17 a declaration about God, 16:19 the command's own seat forward); the Mekhilta: bribery absolute — even to judge truly"), ('MOVE', "Ketubot 105a:10 (read whole at the docket) — 'AND A BRIBE YOU SHALL NOT TAKE' (Exodus 23:8) — what is the verse teaching? if to acquit the guilty and convict the innocent, 16:19 already says 'you shall not wrest judgment': RATHER, EVEN TO ACQUIT THE INNOCENT AND CONVICT THE GUILTY the Torah said 'you shall not take a bribe'; the bribe blinds the eyes of the wise — if the wise, how much more the foolish (I1 — 105a:16, checked in MIDDOT.md)"), ('DATA', 'the exam\'s person: the judge who takes a bribe to judge truly — the rule holds against him (Ketubot 105a:10); the readback row 10:17 (the bribe) VARIANT by CALL; Onkelos "ולא לקבלא שחדא" (and not to receive a