FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_yoke_of_the_commandments) = ("the yoke of the commandments (11:13-21) — THE ANSWER SHEET'S OWN NAME for the paragraph (Mishnah Berakhot 2:2; Berakhot 14b:11 — the yoke of the kingdom of Heaven first, then the yoke of the commandments), typed TEACH AND PERFORM (14b:14): THE WRITE yoke_of_the_commandments_accepted, a STATUS on Israel at the counter's day on the line second_paragraph_declared", ['yoke_of_the_commandments_accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:13-21 — "and it shall be, if you hearken" — the paragraph 11:13-21 the Shema\'s SECOND (6:4-9 the first, Numbers 15:37-41 the third); its duties 6:6-9\'s said again in the plural: "and you shall put these My words" [\'Deut 11:18\'], "and bind them" [\'Deut 11:18\'], "and you shall teach them" [\'Deut 11:19\'], "and you shall write them" [\'Deut 11:20\'] — the consecutive perfects of 11:18-20 {18: [\'ושמתם\', \'וקשרתם\', \'והיו\'], 19: [\'ולמדתם\'], 20: [\'וכתבתם\']}'), ('MOVE', "Mishnah Berakhot 2:2 (credited); Berakhot 14b:11, 14b:12-14, 14b:19, 14b:24 (read whole at the docket) — THE ANSWER SHEET'S OWN NAME FOR THIS PARAGRAPH — R. Yehoshua ben Korcha: why does the Shema precede 'and it shall be, if you hearken'? so that one first accepts THE YOKE OF THE KINGDOM OF HEAVEN and afterward THE YOKE OF THE COMMANDMENTS (Mishnah Berakhot 2:2; the Gemara's citation 14b:11); R. Shimon ben Yochai: the first paragraph learn, teach and perform, THIS PARAGRAPH TEACH AND PERFORM, the third perform alone (14b:12-14 — the order by the directives); Rav's practice — the Shema before the tefillin, the yoke's order applied (14b:19); the Shema without tefillin false testimony against oneself (14b:24, Ulla)"), ('DATA', "THE WRITE yoke_of_the_commandments_accepted — a STATUS on israel_people on the line second_paragraph_declared (the daemon writes it with the two HEAVEN entries): THE NAME FROM THE ANSWER SHEET (7b's lesson 7 — the docket names the effect); the paragraph typed TEACH AND PERFORM —