esign did not predict (the docket\'s crown); the exam\'s person the one who eats before feeding his cattle — accepted against; Onkelos "ואתין עסבא בחקלך לבעירך" (and I will give grass in your field for your cattle)')])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(take_heed_lest) = ("take heed lest (11:16) — 'take heed to yourselves' 4:23's warning form (the three seats), 'serve other gods and bow' the second word's pair in 8:19's order (CH.the_second_word, GL.the_testimony by CALL): the readback row VARIANT; NO second block — other_gods_barred stands at the giving's line", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:16 — "TAKE HEED TO YOURSELVES LEST your heart be deceived and you turn aside and SERVE OTHER GODS AND BOW DOWN TO THEM" — "take heed to yourselves" the three seats [\'Deut 11:16\', \'Deut 4:23\', \'Exod 19:12\'] (4:23 the covenant\'s warning, Exodus 19:12 the mountain\'s); "lest your heart be deceived" the one seat [\'Deut 11:16\']; the four consecutive perfects [\'וסרתם\', \'ועבדתם\', \'והשתחויתם\']; "serve … and bow" the order of 8:19 and 11:16 against the second word\'s "bow … and serve" [\'Deut 5:9\', \'Exod 20:5\']'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_covenant_at_horeb (CALL) — CH.the_second_word(no_other_gods) = no other gods before me (5:7) — the second word's ; CH.the_second_word(bow_and_serve) = bow and serve (5:9) — the bower stoned: the second / fx ['put_to_death']; cold_run_good_land (CALL) — GL.the_testimony(other_gods_serve_bow) = other gods, serve and bow (8:19) — the second word's clause  — the second word's block other_gods_barred on Israel at the giving's line (1, 3, 7) — the bower stoned (Mishnah Sanhedrin 7:6); 8:19's 'serve … and bow' the order reversed: THE WARNING BY 'TAKE HEED' IS NOT A NEW PROHIBITION (4:23's form) — NO SECOND BLOCK at 11:16, other_gods_barred UNMOVED (DC6); the readback row 11:16 VARIANT by CALL"), ('DATA', 'NO second block — other_gods_barred ONE and coveting_barred ONE on israel_people UNMOVED (asserted at DC6); the warning\'s form 4:23\'s; Ahab\'s furrows (Sanhedrin 113a:11) and David\'s famine (Yevamot 78b:14) the run\'s cases — DATA rows; Onkelos "אסתמרו לכון דילמא יטעי לבכון" (take heed to yourselves lest your heart err)')])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_heavens_shut) = ("the heavens shut (11:17) — Leviticus 26:19-20's iron heavens (TC.cascade(1) by CALL — the second block, no line on the tape) told as the shutting: the readback row VARIANT; THE WRITE heavens_shut_for_turning — a conditional HEAVEN entry on Israel, its value THE CLOUDS AND THE WINDS WITHHELD, not rain alone (Ta'anit 3b:6)", ['heavens_shut_for_turning'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:17 — "and the anger of the LORD be kindled against you, and HE SHUT UP THE HEAVENS AND THERE BE NO RAIN, and the ground not give its produce, and you perish quickly from off the good land which the LORD gives you" — "and He shut up the heavens" the one seat [\'Deut 11:17\'] (the lemma\'s Torah seats [(\'Deut 11:17\', \'ועצר\'), (\'Deut 32:36\', \'עצור\'), (\'Gen 16:2\', \'עצרני\'), (\'Gen 20:18\', \'עצר\'), (\'Gen 20:18\', \'עצר\'), (\'Num 17:13\', \'ותעצר\'), (\'Num 17:15\', \'נעצרה\'), (\'Num 25:8\', \'ותעצר\')]); "and the anger of the LORD be kindled against you" the three seats [\'Deut 11:17\', \'Deut 7:4\', \'Josh 23:16\'] (Joshua 23:16 the run\'s receipt); "the ground not give its produce" against Leviticus 26:4\'s "the land shall give its produce" [\'Lev 26:4\'] and 26:20\'s "your land shall not give its produce" [\'Lev 26:20\']; the shared run with Leviticus 26:20 5, Joshua 23:16 11'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_tochacha (CALL) — TC.cascade(1) stage 2, span (19, 20), fx ['chastised_sevenfold']; TC.covenant(False, False, False) = curse_entry — LEVITICUS 26:19-20 — 'I will make your heaven as iron and your earth as brass; your strength shall be spent in vain, your land shall not give its produce' (the cascade's SECOND BLOCK, the gate at 26:18 — chastised_sevenfold; NO LINE ON THE TAPE): the retelling's 'He shut up the heavens' the iron heaven's own word — the readback row 11:17 VARIANT by CALL"), ('MOVE', "Ta'anit 3b:6 (read whole at the docket) — THE SHUTTING'S VALUE — Rav Yosef's baraita: 'and He will shut up the heavens' (11:17) — from THE CLOUDS AND FROM THE WINDS; do you say from the clouds and the winds, or only no rain? when the verse says 'so that there will be no rain', rain is already said — 'shut up the heavens' must mean FROM THE CLOUDS AND THE WINDS: the effect's value, not rain alone"), ('DATA', 'THE WRITE heavens_shut_for_turning — a conditional HEAVEN entry on israel_people on the line second_paragraph_declared: its value the clouds and the winds withheld (Ta\'anit 3b:6 — a DATA row the design did not predict); the readback row 11:17 VARIANT; Onkelos "ויחוד ית שמיא ולא יהי מטרא" (and He will shut the heavens and there will be no rain)')])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_shuttings_threshold) = ("the shutting's threshold (11:17) — rains that seal a barrel's mouth with their mud are not 'shut' (Rav Chisda, Ta'anit 6b:8; the first rainfall a handbreadth, R. Abbahu); the shutting verb the wombs' — closing, birth and remembering said of a woman and of rain (Reish Lakish in bar Kappara's name, 8a:18, 8b:1-3; the Sifrei 306:6)", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:17 — "He shut up the heavens and there be no rain" — the shutting-lemma\'s Bible seats beside the wombs\' [(\'1Chr 12:1\', \'עצור\'), (\'1Chr 21:22\', \'ותעצר\'), (\'1Chr 29:14\', \'נעצר\'), (\'1Kgs 8:35\', \'בהעצר\'), (\'1Kgs 14:10\', \'עצור\'), (\'1Kgs 18:44\', \'יעצרכה\'), (\'1Kgs 21:21\', \'ועצור\'), (\'1Sam 9:17\', \'יעצר\')] (Genesis 20:18 "the LORD had fast closed up all the wombs")'), ('MOVE', "Ta'anit 6b:8; 8a:18, 8b:1-3 (read whole at the docket) — THE THRESHOLD — R. Abbahu: the first rainfall saturates the ground a handbreadth, the second seals a barrel's mouth with its mud; Rav Chisda: rains that seal a barrel's mouth with mud are NOT 'He will shut up the heavens and there will be no rain' (6b:8) — the shutting's measure; THE SHUTTING VERB THE WOMBS' — Reish Lakish: the heavens closed from dew and rain like a woman in labor who cannot give birth; bar Kappara: 'closing' said of rains (11:17) and of a woman (Genesis 20:18), 'giving birth' of a woman (30:23) and of rain (Isaiah 55:10), 'remembering' of Sarah (21:1) and of the earth watered (Psalm 65:10): THREE ANALOGIES (8a:18, 8b:1-3) — the Sifrei 306:6's reading at its Bavli seat (the design's note confirmed)"), ('DATA', "the threshold a PARAMETER row (the barrel's mud) — a DATA row the design did not predict; the wombs' verb the reading's find confirmed at 8b:1 (credited to the Genesis triage, read whole here)")])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_shuttings_causes) = ("the shutting's causes (11:16-17) — the chapter's one cause (other gods) beside the shelf's many (the sentence of destruction from 11:17, the tithes, slander, the impudent, the neglect of Torah, robbery, no whisperers, false pledges — Ta'anit 7b:5-8a:8, 8b:16): a parameter with many arms; the remedy prayer and the pious; the fasts the run's response (10a:16): the community that fasts from Kislev's New Moon accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:16-17 — "lest your heart be deceived and you turn aside and serve other gods … and He shut up the heavens" — THE CHAPTER\'S OWN CAUSE the turning to other gods; "and you perish quickly from off the good land" [\'Deut 11:17\']'), ('MOVE', "Ta'anit 7b:5-8a:8, 8a:14, 8b:16, 10a:16 (read whole at the docket) — THE CAUSES ON THE SHELF — Ze'iri from Dihavat: 'we learned it from here — He will shut up the heavens … and you perish quickly' (11:17 — the sentence of destruction, 7b:5); the tithes annulled (Rav Chisda, 7b:6); slander (7b:7); the impudent (7b:8); dereliction of Torah (7b:10-11); robbery (7b:12); no whisperers of prayer (8a:6); charity pledged in public and not given (8b:16); the faithful alone bring rain (8a:14): THE CAUSE A PARAMETER WITH MANY ARMS beside the chapter's one; THE REMEDY — prayer (7b:13, 7b:15), the generation's most pious (8a:8); THE RUN'S RESPONSE — the fasts from the seventeenth of Marcheshvan (individuals) and the New Moon of Kislev (the court, the community) — Mishnah Ta'anit 1:4-5 through 10a:16"), ('DATA', "the causes a DATA row (a parameter with many arms — the design did not predict); the exam's person the community that fasts from Kislev's New Moon — the court's decree holds: accepted; the remedy prayer")])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(perish_quickly) = ("perish quickly (11:17) — Joshua 23:16's farewell the run's receipt (eleven tokens shared); Solomon's dedication 'when heaven is shut up and there is no rain' (1 Kings 8:35-36 — Ta'anit 7b:4); Ahab's furrows (Sanhedrin 113a:11) and David's famine (Yevamot 78b:14) the effect's run cases", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:17 — "and you PERISH QUICKLY from off the good land which the LORD gives you" — the clause [\'Deut 11:17\']; the shared run with Joshua 23:16 11 (ELEVEN — JOSHUA\'S FAREWELL THE RUN\'S RECEIPT: "the anger of the LORD will be kindled against you and you will perish quickly from off the good land"), with 4:26 6, 2 Chronicles 6:26 5'), ('MOVE', "Ta'anit 7b:4 (read whole at the docket); Sanhedrin 113a:11; Yevamot 78b:14 — SOLOMON'S DEDICATION THE RUN'S RECEIPT — Ze'iri from Dihavat: 'when heaven is shut up and there is no rain, when they sin against You, if they pray toward this place … then You, hear in heaven and forgive … and send rain upon Your land' (1 Kings 8:35-36 — 11:17's 'heaven shut … no rain' in the dedication's words); Ahab to Elijah: Moses' curse unfulfilled — an idol on every furrow and the rain plentiful (Sanhedrin 113a:11 — 1 Kings 17:1's drought the answer); David's famine — perhaps idolaters among you (Yevamot 78b:14): the effect's RUN CASES in the Prophets"), ('DATA', "Joshua 23:16 (eleven tokens), 1 Kings 8:35-36, 17:1, 2 Samuel 21:1 — the run's receipts of heavens_shut_for_turning, DATA rows; the exam's row Solomon's prayer")])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(these_my_words) = ("these My words (11:18) — 'and you shall put these My words on your heart and on your soul' the one seat (6:6's 'and these words shall be' the first paragraph's): the paragraph in any language or as written, not out of order, audible (Sotah 32b:19-33a:4); the readback row VERBATIM in kind against shema_declared (Deut 6:4)", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:18 — "AND YOU SHALL PUT THESE MY WORDS on your heart and on your soul" — the clause the one seat [\'Deut 11:18\'] against 6:6\'s "and these words shall be on your heart" [\'Deut 6:6\']; "on your heart and on your soul" the one seat [\'Deut 11:18\']'), ('MOVE', "Sotah 32b:19, 32b:22-24, 33a:1-4 (read whole at the docket); Kiddushin 30b:3 (credited) — THE PARAGRAPH'S LANGUAGE AND ORDER — the Shema as written (Rabbi) or in any language (the Rabbis — Tosefta 7:7, 32b:19); 'and these words will be' — not out of order (32b:22); audible, 'hear' (32b:24); the whole Torah in any language the inference (33a:1-4); 'you shall put' read 'a perfect elixir' — the bandage on the wound (Kiddushin 30b:3 — chapter 5's docket)"), ('DATA', 'the readback row 11:18 — VERBATIM in kind (shema_declared Deut 6:4 by kind and first verse — the duty \'bind\'); a DATA row: "and you shall put these My words" the one seat; Onkelos "ותשוון ית פתגמי אלין" (and you shall place these My words)')])
