n the runner; the DB plene at 11:18; no change to the DB; the tefillin cell\'s open row STANDS — decision 6); Onkelos "ויהון לתפלין בין עיניכון" (and they shall be tefillin between your eyes)')])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(teach_your_sons) = ("teach your sons (11:19) — 'and you shall teach them' (the piel) against 6:7's 'repeat them': HI.the_four_duties('teach_your_sons', 'daughters_exempt') by CALL — the readback row VARIANT; 'you shall teach them' read 'you yourselves' (Bava Batra 21a:2 — Yehoshua ben Gamla's schools for the fatherless): the father who leaves the teaching to the school accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:19 — "AND YOU SHALL TEACH THEM TO YOUR SONS, speaking of them when you sit in your house and walk on the way and lie down and rise up" — "and you shall teach them to your sons" the one seat [\'Deut 11:19\'] against 6:7\'s "and you shall repeat them to your sons" [\'Deut 6:7\'] (Onkelos\'s two verbs); "and you shall teach" the consecutive perfect\'s seats in the book [(\'Deut 5:1\', \'ולמדתם\'), (\'Deut 11:19\', \'ולמדתם\')]; the shared run with 6:7 7'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_hear_o_israel (CALL) — HI.the_four_duties(teach_your_sons) = teach your sons (6:7) — the father's duty to teach Torah, th; (daughters_exempt) = the daughters (6:7) — 'your sons', not your daughters: the d / fx ['exempt'] — the father's duty to teach Torah, the disciples 'sons' (the Sifrei 34:1; 46:1 'your sons and not your daughters' — Kiddushin 29b credited); Bava Batra 21a:2 (read whole at the docket): 'AND YOU SHALL TEACH THEM' read 'YOU YOURSELVES' shall teach — the do-not-read reading named, no code: the father the teacher; YEHOSHUA BEN GAMLA'S ORDINANCE — the fatherless learned nothing, so schools in every town (the run's institution); Berakhot 15b:27 the teaching complete (credited)"), ('DATA', 'the readback row 11:19 — VARIANT by CALL ("teach" the piel against 6:7\'s "repeat"); the exam\'s person the father who leaves the teaching to the school — the school for the fatherless, the father the teacher: accepted; Onkelos "ותלפון יתהון ית בניכון" (and you shall teach them to your sons)')])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_doorposts_plural) = ("the doorposts plural (11:20) — 'on the doorposts' plural against 6:9's spelling (the Sifrei 36:3's second plural): HI.the_four_duties('mezuzah_doorpost', 'mezuzah_gates', 'mezuzah_writing') by CALL — the readback row VERBATIM in kind; the mezuzah not time-bound, women obligated by the reward clause (Kiddushin 34a:2, 34a:8; Yoma 11b:8): the woman at the mezuzah accepted", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:20 — "AND YOU SHALL WRITE THEM ON THE DOORPOSTS of your house and on your gates" — the PLURAL "doorposts" here [\'Deut 11:20\'] against 6:9\'s SINGULAR-SPELLED "doorpost" [\'Deut 6:9\'] (the lemma\'s book seats [(\'Deut 6:9\', \'מזוזת\'), (\'Deut 11:20\', \'מזוזות\')] — the Sifrei 36:3\'s second plural); the shared run with 6:9 4'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_hear_o_israel (CALL) — HI.the_four_duties(mezuzah_doorpost) = the doorpost (6:9) — one post, the right as one en; (mezuzah_gates) = the gates (6:9) — the dwelling's, not the bathhous / fx ['exempt']; (mezuzah_writing) = the mezuzah's writing (6:9) — a scroll in ink with — one post, the right as one enters, the upper third; the dwelling's gates, not the bathhouse's (its owner exempt); a scroll in ink, not the stones: the readback row 11:20 VERBATIM in kind by CALL; Kiddushin 34a:2 and 34a:8, Yoma 11b:8 (read whole at the docket): THE MEZUZAH NOT TIME-BOUND — WOMEN OBLIGATED, the reward clause 'that your days be multiplied' (11:21) deciding against the juxtaposition to study ('do men need life and women not?')"), ('DATA', 'the doorposts\' two plurals the DATA row (the reading\'s find; the Sifrei 36:3); the exam\'s person the woman at the mezuzah — obligated: accepted; Onkelos "על מזוזין" (on the doorposts)')])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_days_multiplied) = ("the days multiplied (11:21) — 'as the days of the heavens above the earth' the one seat; 6:2's three generations by CALL (HI.the_header): the readback row VARIANT; the resurrection from 'to give to them' (the Sifrei 47:2; Sanhedrin 90b:12), the messianic era's measure (99a:10), lengthened in the Land (Berakhot 8a:6), the adjacency's reach (Shabbat 32b:4 — E28)", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:21 — "THAT YOUR DAYS AND THE DAYS OF YOUR SONS BE MULTIPLIED on the land which the LORD swore to your fathers TO GIVE TO THEM, AS THE DAYS OF THE HEAVENS ABOVE THE EARTH" — "that your days be multiplied" the one seat [\'Deut 11:21\']; "as the days of the heavens above the earth" the one seat [\'Deut 11:21\'] (Psalm 89:30 "as the days of heaven" [\'Ps 89:30\']); "which the LORD swore to your fathers to give to them" the two seats [\'Deut 11:21\', \'Deut 11:9\'] (11:9, 11:21); the shared run with 11:9 8'), ('MOVE', "cold_run_hear_o_israel (CALL) — HI.the_header(your_sons_son) = your son's son (6:2) — three generations in the fear; Exodus — 6:2's three generations in the fear: the readback row 11:21 VARIANT by CALL; THE RESURRECTION FROM 'TO THEM' — 'to give to them', not 'to you': the fathers rise to receive it (the Sifrei 47:2; Sanhedrin 90b:12 credited from the Devarim docket); the messianic era as long as from creation to now, 'as the days of the heavens' (Sanhedrin 99a:10); lengthened in the Land and not outside — R. Yochanan on the elders of Babylonia (Berakhot 8a:6); 'a blessing is different', many days AND years (Shabbat 105b:11); 'your sons' inclusive at the reward — daughters too (Bava Batra 110b:7); children die for the mezuzah's neglect or the study's — the adjacency's reach (Shabbat 32b:4, E28 — checked in MIDDOT.md)"), ('DATA', 'the readback row 11:21 — VARIANT by CALL (HI.the_header); the resurrection\'s seat "to them" a DATA row; the dead outside the Land (Ketubot 111a:16-21) the seat\'s edge; Onkelos "כיומי שמיא על ארעא" (as the days of the heavens above the earth)')])
FACT blessing_and_curse.the_second_paragraph(the_class_rule) = ("the class rule (11:18-20) — Mishnah Kiddushin 1:7 behind the paragraph's duties: the tefillin time-bound (women exempt — 36a:9), the mezuzah not (women obligated by the reward — 34a:2, 34a:8; Yoma 11b:8), the study the son's (daughters exempt — HI by CALL); the skull that never donned tefillin the body's rebellion (Rosh Hashanah 17a:10): accepted against", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 11:18-20 — "bind them … frontlets … teach them to your sons … write them on the doorposts" — the paragraph\'s three duties said to the plural: the second person PLURAL in verses 18-20 {18: (6, 0), 19: (2, 5), 20: (0, 3)}'), ('MOVE', "Mishnah Kiddushin 1:7 (read whole at the docket); Kiddushin 34a:2, 34a:8, 36a:9; Yoma 11b:8; Rosh Hashanah 17a:10 — THE CLASS RULE BEHIND THE PARAGRAPH'S DUTIES — the son's duties on the father: men obligated, women exempt; the father's on the son: both; positive time-bound: men; not time-bound: both; prohibitions: both (Mishnah Kiddushin 1:7): THE TEFILLIN time-bound — women exempt (and the baldness bar with them, 36a:9); THE MEZUZAH not time-bound — women obligated (34a:2), the reward clause deciding (34a:8; Yoma 11b:8); THE STUDY the son's — daughters exempt (HI.the_four_duties('daughters_exempt') = the daughters (6:7) — 'your sons', not y); THE SKULL THAT NEVER DONNED TEFILLIN the body's rebellion (Rav — Rosh Hashanah 17a:10)"), ('DATA', "the answer sheet for the_four_duties by CALL (Mishnah Kiddushin 1:7 the class rule) — a DATA row; the exam's person the skull that never donned tefillin — the rebellious with his body: accepted against")])
