nt in pledge' — a widow, rich or poor, is not pledged (Bava Metzia 9:13 — the Exodus cell READ 24:17 FORWARD, 'Deut 24:17 [IMPORT]' in its why; 281:3 cites nothing — the reading's twenty-one); 10:18's orphan and widow Exodus 22:21's pair (second_tablets by CALL)"), ('DATA', "THE WRITES stranger_orphan_justice_commanded (a STATUS) and widows_garment_pledge_barred (a BLOCK) on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DK2); the_prohibitions_count a DATA row (two for the sojourner, three for the sojourner-orphan — 281:1-2); judgment_wresting_barred the reference; the exam's person the creditor who pledges a rich widow's garment — barred, rich or poor")])
