FACT courts_prophet.the_king(set_you_shall_set) = ("set, you shall set (17:15) — succession by the doubled verb, a king and not a queen, a positive command (the Sifrei 157:1-2, 157:7; the kings promised ['ומלכים'] and Judah's scepter by CALL — the tape's references): THE WRITE king_from_the_brothers_commanded, a STATUS on Israel at the chapters' own day; the people who set a queen barred from it", ['king_from_the_brothers_commanded'], [('INK', 'Deut 17:15 — "SET, YOU SHALL SET A KING OVER YOU whom the LORD your God will choose" — the doubled verb [\'שום\', \'תשים\', \'תשים\']; "a king" [\'מלך\', \'מלך\']; kings_promised on jacob [\'jacob\'] and prophet_declared on abraham [\'abraham\'] the tape\'s entries'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 157:1-2, 157:7 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_pre_sinai (CALL) — PS_.circumcision(kings) = [(6, ['ומלכים']), (16, ['מלכי'])]; cold_run_balak (CALL) — BK.judah_blessing = ['oracle_blessed'] — 'SET, YOU SHALL SET' — IF HE DIED, APPOINT ANOTHER IN HIS PLACE (157:1 — the doubled verb succession, the office continuous; 162:4 the son); 'a king' — and not a queen (157:2); another word: 'set, you shall set' — a positive commandment (157:7); Genesis 17:6, 17:16's 'kings shall come from you' and 35:11's promise (a heaven entry on Jacob) and 49:10's scepter (balak's Judah) THE TAPE'S REFERENCES"), ('DATA', "THE WRITE king_from_the_brothers_commanded — a STATUS on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DI2); the office male, continuous; the exam's person the people who set a queen — barred from it")])
FACT courts_prophet.the_king(chosen_by_a_prophet) = ("chosen by a prophet (17:15) — 'whom the LORD will choose' by the mouth of a prophet: chapter 18's prophet the selector of chapter 17's king (the Sifrei 157:3): the people who crown without a prophet's word accepted against", ['accepted'], [('INK', 'Deut 17:15 — "whom the LORD your God WILL CHOOSE" — "will choose" [\'יבחר\'] (the place formula\'s verb at the king); 18:15\'s prophet the selector'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 157:3 (read whole at the reading) — 'WHOM THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL CHOOSE' — BY THE MOUTH OF A PROPHET (157:3): THE KING'S CHOICE THROUGH THE PROPHET — chapter 18's prophet (F8) the instrument of chapter 17's king (Samuel and Saul, Samuel and David the run's future cases): the two cells' one edge inside the runner"), ('DATA', "chosen by a prophet a DATA row (the choice's instrument F8's prophet; the tape's future cases Samuel's); the exam's person the people who crown a king without a prophet's word — accepted against")])
FACT courts_prophet.the_king(from_among_your_brothers_and_agrippas) = ("from among your brothers and Agrippas (17:15) — not from outside the land, not from others, the foreigner a prohibition (the Sifrei 157:4-5, 157:8-9); Agrippas weeping and Israel's 'you are our brother' (157:10 = Mishnah Sotah 7:8 — the exam row read whole): THE WRITE foreign_king_barred, a BLOCK on Israel at the chapters' own day; the people who set a foreigner barred from it", ['foreign_king_barred'], [('INK', 'Deut 17:15 — "FROM AMONG YOUR BROTHERS you shall set a king over you; YOU MAY NOT SET OVER YOU A FOREIGNER who is not your brother" — "you may not" [\'לא\', \'תוכל\', \'לא\'] (Onkelos "you have no permission" — the book\'s four seats, the reading\'s assert); "from among your brothers" one seat in the Bible'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 157:4-5, 157:8-10 (read whole at the reading — the Mishnah cited in the spine's Hebrew); MISHNAH SOTAH 7:8 (read whole at the design — THE EXAM ROW) — 'FROM AMONG' — not from outside the land; 'YOUR BROTHERS' — not from others (157:4-5); 'you may not set a foreigner' — a negative commandment (157:8); 'a foreign MAN' — a man is appointed provider over the community, a woman is not (157:9); WHEN AGRIPPAS REACHED THIS VERSE HE WEPT, AND ALL ISRAEL SAID: FEAR NOT, AGRIPPAS, YOU ARE OUR BROTHER (157:10 = Sotah 7:8 — the king's portion at the assembly, the scroll passed from the attendant to the head to the deputy to the high priest to the king, standing to receive and reading standing, praised)"), ('DATA', "THE WRITE foreign_king_barred — a BLOCK on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DI2); the king's reading at the assembly a DATA row (Sotah 7:8 — the portions read); the exam's person the people who set a foreigner — barred from it; Agrippas the row's own case, 'our brother'")])
FACT courts_prophet.the_king(the_awe_of_the_king) = ("the awe of the king (17:15, 17:19) — none ride his horse nor sit on his throne (the Sifrei 157:6 — Sanhedrin 2:5); the road without measure, the first share (161:4 = Mishnah Sanhedrin 2:4 — the exam row read whole): a PARAMETER; the one who rides the king's horse barred from it", ['barred_from_it'], [('INK', 'Deut 17:15, 17:19 — "you shall set a king over you" said again — "that his awe be upon you"; "and it shall be with him" [\'והיתה\', \'עמו\']'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 157:6, 161:4 (read whole at the reading — the Mishnah cited in the spine's Hebrew); MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 2:4 (read whole at the design — THE EXAM ROW) — WHY 'YOU SHALL SET A KING OVER YOU' AGAIN? THAT HIS AWE BE UPON YOU — from here they said: a king — none ride his horse, sit on his throne, use his sceptre, see him naked or at the barber or in the bath (157:6 — Sanhedrin 2:5 by 'from here they said'); A KING BREAKS THROUGH TO MAKE HIMSELF A ROAD AND NONE PROTEST, the king's road has no measure, all the people plunder and set it before him and he takes the first share (161:4 = Sanhedrin 2:4's head — the optional war by the seventy-one the row's own clause)"), ('DATA', "THE PARAMETER the_kings_awe (the six of Sanhedrin 2:5; the road without measure and the first share of Sanhedrin 2:4); the exam's person the one who rides the king's horse — barred from it")])
FACT courts_prophet.the_king(the_three_limits_for_himself) = ("the three limits for himself (17:16-17) — the chariot's horses and the army's treasury allowed, the idle horse, eighteen wives or the heart or Abigail, the soldiers' pay, David and Solomon (the Sifrei 158:1-159:4 = Mishnah Sanhedrin 2:4 — the exam row read whole; good_land's twin by CALL): THE WRITES horses_multiplying_barred, return_to_egypt_barred, wives_multiplying_barred, silver_and_gold_multiplying_barred, BLOCKS on Israel at the chapters' own day; the king who keeps horses beyond his chariot barred from it", ['horses_multiplying_barred', 'return_to_egypt_barred', 'wives_multiplying_barred', 'silver_and_gold_multiplying_barred'], [('INK', 'Deut 17:16-17 — "ONLY HE SHALL NOT MULTIPLY HORSES FOR HIMSELF, nor return the people to Egypt in order to multiply horse, since the LORD said to you: you shall not return that way again; AND HE SHALL NOT MULTIPLY WIVES FOR HIMSELF, that his heart turn not; AND SILVER AND GOLD HE SHALL NOT MULTIPLY GREATLY FOR HIMSELF" — "for himself" three times [(16, \'לו\'), (17, \'לו\'), (17, \'לו\')]; "horses" and "horse" [\'סוסים\', \'סוס\']; 8:13\'s silver and gold the twin (shared 3 — good_land)'), ('MOVE', 'the Sifrei 158:1-4, 159:1-4 (read whole at the reading — the Mishnah cited in the spine\'s Hebrew at 161:1); MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 2:4 (read whole at the design — THE EXAM ROW); cold_run_good_land (CALL) — GL.DATA[the_kings_law_tokens] = {\'silver_and_gold\': "8:13 \'and your silver and gold SHALL MULTIPLY\' /  — \'FOR HIMSELF\' SPLITS EACH LIMIT — for himself not, for his chariots and horsemen he may (158:1 — Sanhedrin 2:4: enough for his chariot); \'horse\' the idle beast (158:2); EVEN ONE IDLE HORSE ENOUGH TO RETURN THE PEOPLE TO EGYPT (158:3); the a fortiori to every land (158:4 — I1); \'wives\' — BUT EIGHTEEN (159:1 — Sanhedrin 2:4); R. Judah: he may multiply provided they do not turn his heart; R. Simeon: even one who turns his heart, and \'he shall not multiply\' even Abigail and her companions (159:2-3 — THREE ARMS on the Mishnah\'s own line); \'silver and gold\' — for himself not, for the army he may (159:4 — Sanhedrin 2:4: the soldiers\' pay); DAVID KEPT IT AND SOLOMON CHANGED IT (1 Chronicles 22:14, 1 Kings 10:27 — the run\'s future case); \'since the LORD said to you\' A RECEIPT BEHIND — Exodus 14:13\'s clause inside the tape\'s Exodus 14 scene (no own line; Sukkah 51b\'s reading not read)'), ('DATA', "THE WRITES horses_multiplying_barred, return_to_egypt_barred, wives_multiplying_barred, silver_and_gold_multiplying_barred — BLOCKS on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DI2); THE PARAMETER the_three_limits (Sanhedrin 2:4: eighteen wives with three arms, the chariot's horses, the soldiers' pay; the idle horse); Solomon the readback's future exercise; the exam's person the king who keeps horses beyond his chariot — barred from it")])
FACT courts_prophet.the_king(the_copy_of_the_law) = ("the copy of the law (17:18-19) — his own, the whole Torah, on a scroll of clean skin corrected by the seventy-one, with him in war, in judgment, at table, the nights too (the Sifrei 160:1-8, 161:1-2 = Mishnah Sanhedrin 2:4 — the exam row read whole): THE WRITE law_copy_commanded, a STATUS on Israel at the chapters' own day; the king who reads his father's scroll barred from it", ['law_copy_commanded'], [('INK', 'Deut 17:18-19 — "and when he sits on the throne of his kingdom, HE SHALL WRITE FOR HIMSELF A COPY OF THIS LAW ON A BOOK from before the priests the Levites; and it shall be with him and he shall read in it ALL THE DAYS OF HIS LIFE" — "a copy of this law" [\'משנה\', \'התורה\']; "all the days of his life" [\'כל\', \'ימי\', \'חייו\', \'כל\']'), ('MOVE', "the Sifrei 160:1-8, 161:1-2 (read whole at the reading — the Mishnah cited in the spine's Hebrew at 161:1); MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 2:4 (read whole at the design — THE EXAM ROW) — worthy of the throne when he does all said in the matter (160:1); 'for himself' — for his own name, never his fathers' (160:2); 'a copy' — only Deuteronomy? 'to keep all the words of this law' — the whole Torah; why 'the copy'? because it was to be changed, the script (160:3); the assembly day reads only the copy (160:4); 'ON A BOOK' — not a tablet, not paper, but a scroll, of a clean beast's skin, CORRECTED FROM THE COURTYARD'S SCROLL BY THE COURT OF SEVENTY-ONE (160:5-7); the Torah destined to be forgotten (160:8 — R. Elazar ben Arakh); THE KING GOES OUT TO WAR AND IT IS WITH HIM, comes in and it is with him, sits in judgment and it is beside him, reclines and it is before him (161:1 = Sanhedrin 2:4); 'the days of his life' the days, 'ALL the days' the nights (161:2 — Berakhot 1:5's move, chapter 16's exam row)"), ('DATA', "THE WRITE law_copy_commanded — a STATUS on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DI2) — the king's own ledger a FUTURE entity's; THE PARAMETER the_copys_form (a scroll of clean skin, his own, corrected by the seventy-one, with him always); the exam's person the king who reads his father's scroll — barred from it")])
FACT courts_prophet.the_king(the_circle_of_learning_and_the_heart) = ("the circle of learning and the heart (17:19-20) — fear to Scripture to deed to fear; the heart not above the brothers nor the consecrated; the days conditioned; the son in his place (the Sifrei 161:3, 162:1-5; good_land's 8:14 twin by CALL): THE WRITE heart_lifting_barred, a BLOCK on Israel at the chapters' own day; the king whose heart is lifted barred from it", ['heart_lifting_barred'], [('INK', 'Deut 17:19-20 — "that he may learn to fear the LORD his God … THAT HIS HEART BE NOT LIFTED ABOVE HIS BROTHERS, and that he turn not from the commandment right or left, that he may prolong days over his kingdom, he and his sons" — "his heart" [\'לבבו\']; 8:14\'s "your heart be lifted" the twin (shared 0 — good_land)'), ('MOVE', 'the Sifrei 161:3, 161:5, 162:1-5 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_good_land (CALL) — GL.DATA[the_heart_lifted] = {\'denial\': "Sotah 4b:11 — R. Yochanan: the arrogant DENIES t — \'THAT HE MAY LEARN TO FEAR\' — FEAR BRINGS TO SCRIPTURE, SCRIPTURE TO TRANSLATION, TRANSLATION TO MISHNAH, MISHNAH TO TALMUD, TALMUD TO DEED, DEED TO FEAR; the commoner equals the king in Torah, not in other things (161:3); \'these statutes\' — the statutes of kingship (161:5 — a second reading); \'not lifted above his brothers\' — and not above the consecrated (162:1); \'lest\' rendered \'that he not turn\' (162:2); worthy to prolong days if he does what is written (162:3); \'he and his sons\' — his son stands in his place, and every provider\'s (162:4); Solomon\'s unasked riches against the conditioned days (162:5 — 1 Kings 3:13-14); the arrogant as an idolater (Sotah 4b — good_land\'s row by CALL)'), ('DATA', "THE WRITE heart_lifting_barred — a BLOCK on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DI2); THE PARAMETER the_circle_of_learning (fear to Scripture to translation to Mishnah to Talmud to deed to fear); succession the son's for every office; the exam's person the king whose heart is lifted above his brothers — barred from it")])
